From 4efd2e53b227db1aaf331c0230f6e2c55b65f7f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: REPLACE WITH PEM120 REAL NAME <replace-me@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 05:07:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Input: atmel_mxt_ts - read the info block checksum separately

The touch controller on a Xiaomi Mi 4i (ferrari) with a replacement
display panel identifies itself as an mXT336T (family 0xa4, variant
0x15, firmware 2.1.AA, 41 objects), but its I2C interface does not
behave like a genuine maXTouch: reads that do not start at one of a few
special addresses return bytes from a flat 256-byte map indexed by the
low address byte. It appears to be firmware that emulates the maXTouch
object protocol.

When the object table and the info block checksum are read in a single
transfer starting at MXT_OBJECT_START, this controller returns the
object table correctly but 00 00 fc in place of the checksum, and probe
fails with "Info Block CRC error". A separate read of the three checksum
bytes returns 0x8DDD0D, which matches the checksum calculated over the
ID information and the object table. The Xiaomi vendor driver also reads
the checksum on its own.

Read the checksum in its own transfer, just as the ID information is
already read separately from the object table. The checksum is still
calculated and verified over the same contiguous buffer, so the check
added by commit 068bdb67ef74 ("Input: atmel_mxt_ts - fix the firmware
update") is unchanged, and a genuine controller returns the same bytes
either way. The cost is one extra 3-byte read at probe.

Also skip the object table transfer if the info block reports no
objects, so that no zero-length read is issued.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/atmel_mxt_ts.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/atmel_mxt_ts.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/atmel_mxt_ts.c
index 2c0e5a6713..76589ac39e 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/atmel_mxt_ts.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/atmel_mxt_ts.c
@@ -1875,10 +1875,24 @@ static int mxt_read_info_block(struct mxt_data *data)
 
 	id_buf = buf;
 
-	/* Read rest of info block */
-	error = __mxt_read_reg(client, MXT_OBJECT_START,
-			       size - MXT_OBJECT_START,
-			       id_buf + MXT_OBJECT_START);
+	/*
+	 * Read the object table and the info block checksum in two
+	 * transfers. Some controllers (e.g. the one fitted to Xiaomi Mi 4i
+	 * replacement panels) return garbage for the checksum when it is
+	 * read as the tail of the object table transfer, while a separate
+	 * read of the checksum returns the correct value.
+	 */
+	if (num_objects) {
+		error = __mxt_read_reg(client, MXT_OBJECT_START,
+				       num_objects * sizeof(struct mxt_object),
+				       id_buf + MXT_OBJECT_START);
+		if (error)
+			return error;
+	}
+
+	error = __mxt_read_reg(client, size - MXT_INFO_CHECKSUM_SIZE,
+			       MXT_INFO_CHECKSUM_SIZE,
+			       id_buf + size - MXT_INFO_CHECKSUM_SIZE);
 	if (error)
 		return error;
 

